node-red-contrib-home-connect

Independent, unofficial community software for the public Home Connect API and an experimental, undocumented local appliance protocol.
Inspired at a conceptual level by the discovery-first and safeguarded-write approach of:
https://github.com/impact0815/node-red-contrib-viessmann
No source code from that project is included.

Home Connect and appliance brand names are trademarks of their respective owners. Their use identifies API compatibility only and does not imply affiliation, endorsement or support.

Local protocol behavior was independently implemented using public community observations and documentation from:
https://github.com/chris-mc1/homeconnect_local_hass
https://github.com/chris-mc1/homeconnect_websocket
https://github.com/hcpy2-0/hcpy
https://github.com/zibous/homeconnect-hcpy
https://github.com/Asmir1975/homeconnect_local_hass-UI
https://github.com/SukramJ/go-homeconnect2mqtt
https://github.com/bruestel/homeconnect-profile-downloader

No source code, appliance profiles, credentials, serial numbers, PSKs or IVs from those projects are included. Those projects remain subject to their own licenses; users must review them when installing or using the separate tools.
